node_modules/
dist/
.astro/
.wrangler/

# Secrets - never commit. .env.example is the committed template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Palate: DERIVED state is ignored, MEASURED state is committed. The distinction
# matters. The index is a pure function of the repo and is rebuilt in
# milliseconds, so committing it just makes every rebuild show up as a diff.
# Baselines are the opposite: they record what this site looked like last time,
# which cannot be recomputed from source, and they are the comparison point
# drift is measured against. Ignore them and every contribution looks like the
# first one.
# DERIVED: regenerated by re-running the tool, and large. A real client build committed
# 387 of these into its deliverable repo, 297MB of it screenshots, because only the first
# two lines of this block existed. scripts/palate-gitignore.sh writes the same rules at the
# repo root when git lives one level above this file, which is the other half of that bug.
build-manifest.json
build-manifest.json.*.json
.palate-skill-state.json
.palate-shots/
verify-report.json
.palate/index.json
.palate/*.log
.palate/*.backup.json
.palate/mcp-journal.jsonl
.palate/harvest/
.palate/live-capture/
# Adoption captures a full-page PNG per route plus a filmstrip; one real adoption staged
# 874MB of them. The adoption RECORD beside them (report.json, routes.json) is measured state
# and stays committed, so this ignores the images and not the directory.
.palate/adoption/**/*.png
.palate/adoption/filmstrip/
.palate/tmp/
.palate/explore/shots/
# The Explore SEED is the operator's own drawing work: one hand-authored artboard per rung
# (`B<n>.dc.html`) and the images beside it. Those ARE the directions the client was shown and
# nothing can regenerate them, so they stay COMMITTED. Only what boards-render writes into the
# same directory is ignored, and it writes the calibration row as well as canvas.json: one
# `Ref<n>.dc.html` and one `ref<n>.jpg` per reference, both re-derived from refs.json on every
# run.
.palate/explore/seed/canvas.json
.palate/explore/seed/README.md
.palate/explore/seed/Ref*.dc.html
.palate/explore/seed/ref*.jpg
# The donor row and the board judge are generated the same way: one `D<rung>.dc.html` card and
# one `d<rung>-hero.jpg` per rung, re-fetched from donor-heroes.json on every run, and the
# judge's request and answers, restated on every run and refused once stale. donor-heroes.json
# itself is MEASURED state (the surveyor paid for it) and stays committed.
.palate/explore/seed/D*.dc.html
.palate/explore/seed/d[0-9]*-hero.jpg
.palate/explore/judge-request.json
.palate/explore/judgements.json
public/_explore/
*.palate-bak
.palate-devserver.log
.palate-devserver.pid
# MEASURED state stays committed and is deliberately absent above: baselines, the brand
# record, assets.json (it carries the human photo review), the briefs, the donor lineage.
!.palate/baselines/
!.palate/brain/

.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Vercel local link + creds
.vercel/

# Vercel preview protection-bypass secret (grants access; never commit)
.jiffi-vercel-bypass
